tasks.prompt:
For the acute triangle $\triangle ABC$ it is given that $AC = 13\ \text{cm}$ and $BC = 15\ \text{cm}$. If $CD$ $(D \in AB)$ is an altitude and $AD = 5\ \text{cm}$, find:

A) the perimeter of $\triangle ABC$;

B) the area of $\triangle ABC$;

C) the radius of the circle circumscribed about $\triangle ABC$;

D) the radius of the circle inscribed in $\triangle ABC$.
